# `$` not starting `$left`/`$right`, a lone `&`, and `@` not followed by a quote.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where $foo & x;
@x
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..23
  PIPELINE@0..18
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..9
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
    WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
    ERROR@10..18
      ERROR@10..11 "$"
      IDENT@11..14 "foo"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      ERROR@15..16 "&"
      WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
      IDENT@17..18 "x"
  SEMICOLON@18..19 ";"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"
  ERROR@20..22
    ERROR@20..21 "@"
    IDENT@21..22 "x"
  WHITESPACE@22..23 "\n"

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `$`
  --> query:1:11
  |
1 | t | where $foo & x;
  |           ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: `$` is only used in `$left` and `$right`

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `&`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | t | where $foo & x;
  |                ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: to combine conditions, use `and`

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `@`
  --> query:2:1
  |
2 | @x
  | ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: a verbatim string is `@` followed directly by a quote: `@'C:\data'`
